IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `epd-nouns`
IMPORT `epd-art13`

-- Tests for Article 13. Expected values were decided from the text before the run and are written beside the assertion.
-- Two test-only helpers keep the long calls readable and every argument named:
--   `soft opt-in with limb n flipped`: all twelve soft-opt-in facts satisfied, except the limb numbered n (0 = none flipped).
--   limbs: 1 obtained from its customer, 2 in the context of a sale, 3 in accordance with Directive 95/46/EC, 4 same person,
--   5 own products or services, 6 similar, 7 clearly and distinctly, 8 free of charge, 9 easy manner, 10 at the time of
--   collection, 11 customer initially refused (flipped = TRUE), 12 on the occasion of each message.
--   `case`: the whole-Article question with the soft opt-in and the paragraph 4 features summarised by one yes/no each.

GIVEN means IS A `Marketing means`
      n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`soft opt-in with limb n flipped` MEANS
    `Art 13(2) the soft opt-in applies` WITH
        means IS means
        `the sender obtained the recipient's electronic contact details from its customer` IS (NOT (n EQUALS 1))
        `the details were obtained in the context of the sale of a product or a service` IS (NOT (n EQUALS 2))
        `the details were obtained in accordance with Directive 95/46/EC` IS (NOT (n EQUALS 3))
        `the sender is the same natural or legal person that obtained the details` IS (NOT (n EQUALS 4))
        `the marketing is of the sender's own products or services` IS (NOT (n EQUALS 5))
        `the products or services marketed are similar to those sold to the customer` IS (NOT (n EQUALS 6))
        `the customer was clearly and distinctly given the opportunity to object` IS (NOT (n EQUALS 7))
        `the opportunity to object was free of charge` IS (NOT (n EQUALS 8))
        `the opportunity to object was in an easy manner` IS (NOT (n EQUALS 9))
        `the opportunity to object was given at the time the details were collected` IS (NOT (n EQUALS 10))
        `the customer initially refused such use` IS (n EQUALS 11)
        `the opportunity to object was given on the occasion of each message` IS (NOT (n EQUALS 12))

GIVEN means IS A `Marketing means`
      dm IS A BOOLEAN
      unsolicited IS A BOOLEAN
      natural IS A BOOLEAN
      consent IS A BOOLEAN
      soft IS A BOOLEAN
      ban IS A BOOLEAN
      option IS A `Article 13(3) national option`
      wishes IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
case MEANS
    `Art 13 the message may be sent to the recipient` WITH
        means IS means
        `the message is for the purposes of direct marketing` IS dm
        `the message is unsolicited` IS unsolicited
        `the recipient is a natural person` IS natural
        `the subscriber or user gave their consent before the message was sent` IS consent
        `the sender obtained the recipient's electronic contact details from its customer` IS soft
        `the details were obtained in the context of the sale of a product or a service` IS TRUE
        `the details were obtained in accordance with Directive 95/46/EC` IS TRUE
        `the sender is the same natural or legal person that obtained the details` IS TRUE
        `the marketing is of the sender's own products or services` IS TRUE
        `the products or services marketed are similar to those sold to the customer` IS TRUE
        `the customer was clearly and distinctly given the opportunity to object` IS TRUE
        `the opportunity to object was free of charge` IS TRUE
        `the opportunity to object was in an easy manner` IS TRUE
        `the opportunity to object was given at the time the details were collected` IS TRUE
        `the customer initially refused such use` IS FALSE
        `the opportunity to object was given on the occasion of each message` IS TRUE
        `the message disguises or conceals the identity of the sender on whose behalf it is sent` IS ban
        `the message contravenes Article 6 of Directive 2000/31/EC` IS FALSE
        `the message has no valid address to which the recipient may send a request that such communications cease` IS FALSE
        `the message encourages recipients to visit websites that contravene that Article` IS FALSE
        option IS option
        `the recipient does not wish to receive these communications` IS wishes

§ `Art 13(1)`
--  ruler: the means, direct marketing
#ASSERT `Art 13(1) the use of the means is one that paragraph 1 names` `an automated calling and communication system without human intervention` TRUE  EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 13(1) the use of the means is one that paragraph 1 names` `a facsimile machine` TRUE  EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 13(1) the use of the means is one that paragraph 1 names` `an electronic mail message` TRUE  EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 13(1) the use of the means is one that paragraph 1 names` `another means of communication` TRUE  EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 13(1) the use of the means is one that paragraph 1 names` `an electronic mail message` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
--  ruler: the means, direct marketing, prior consent
#ASSERT `Art 13(1) the use of the means may be allowed in respect of the subscriber or user` `an electronic mail message` TRUE  TRUE  EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 13(1) the use of the means may be allowed in respect of the subscriber or user` `a facsimile machine` TRUE  TRUE  EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 13(1) the use of the means may be allowed in respect of the subscriber or user` `an automated calling and communication system without human intervention` TRUE  TRUE  EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "only in respect of subscribers or users who have given their prior consent": without it the text says no
#ASSERT `Art 13(1) the use of the means may be allowed in respect of the subscriber or user` `an electronic mail message` TRUE  FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 13(1) the use of the means may be allowed in respect of the subscriber or user` `a facsimile machine` TRUE  FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 13(1) the use of the means may be allowed in respect of the subscriber or user` `an automated calling and communication system without human intervention` TRUE  FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- another means, or not direct marketing: paragraph 1 is silent
#ASSERT `Art 13(1) the use of the means may be allowed in respect of the subscriber or user` `another means of communication` TRUE  FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 13(1) the use of the means may be allowed in respect of the subscriber or user` `an electronic mail message` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Art 13(2) the soft opt-in`
#ASSERT `soft opt-in with limb n flipped` `an electronic mail message` 0  EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the three "where" conditions fail: the text says no (periods ruling (b)), a marginal reading
#ASSERT `soft opt-in with limb n flipped` `an electronic mail message` 1  EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `soft opt-in with limb n flipped` `an electronic mail message` 2  EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `soft opt-in with limb n flipped` `an electronic mail message` 3  EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the grant's own limits: the same person, own, similar
#ASSERT `soft opt-in with limb n flipped` `an electronic mail message` 4  EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `soft opt-in with limb n flipped` `an electronic mail message` 5  EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `soft opt-in with limb n flipped` `an electronic mail message` 6  EQUALS NOTHING
-- "provided that" the opportunity to object is given: each element, then the two moments
#ASSERT `soft opt-in with limb n flipped` `an electronic mail message` 7  EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `soft opt-in with limb n flipped` `an electronic mail message` 8  EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `soft opt-in with limb n flipped` `an electronic mail message` 9  EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `soft opt-in with limb n flipped` `an electronic mail message` 10 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `soft opt-in with limb n flipped` `an electronic mail message` 12 EQUALS NOTHING
-- the customer initially refused such use: the text is silent
#ASSERT `soft opt-in with limb n flipped` `an electronic mail message` 11 EQUALS NOTHING
-- the grant is read as covering electronic mail messages only
#ASSERT `soft opt-in with limb n flipped` `a facsimile machine` 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `soft opt-in with limb n flipped` `an automated calling and communication system without human intervention` 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `soft opt-in with limb n flipped` `another means of communication` 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- the "where" gate comes first, for any means
#ASSERT `soft opt-in with limb n flipped` `a facsimile machine` 1 EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Art 13(1) and (2) together`
--  ruler: means, direct marketing, prior consent, then the twelve soft-opt-in facts (obtained, sale, 95/46, same, own, similar, clearly, free, easy, at collection, initially refused, each message)
#ASSERT `Art 13(1) and (2) the use of the means may be allowed in respect of the subscriber or user` `an electronic mail message` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no consent, soft opt-in satisfied: paragraph 2 "notwithstanding paragraph 1"
#ASSERT `Art 13(1) and (2) the use of the means may be allowed in respect of the subscriber or user` `an electronic mail message` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no consent, one soft-opt-in limb missing (each message): paragraph 1's "only" stands
#ASSERT `Art 13(1) and (2) the use of the means may be allowed in respect of the subscriber or user` `an electronic mail message` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- no consent, soft-opt-in facts for a fax: the grant is for electronic mail, so paragraph 1's "only" stands
#ASSERT `Art 13(1) and (2) the use of the means may be allowed in respect of the subscriber or user` `a facsimile machine` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 13(1) and (2) the use of the means may be allowed in respect of the subscriber or user` `another means of communication` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 13(1) and (2) the use of the means may be allowed in respect of the subscriber or user` `an electronic mail message` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Art 13(3)`
--  ruler: the means, unsolicited, direct marketing
#ASSERT `Art 13(3) paragraph 3 applies to the communication` `another means of communication` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 13(3) paragraph 3 applies to the communication` `an electronic mail message` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 13(3) paragraph 3 applies to the communication` `a facsimile machine` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 13(3) paragraph 3 applies to the communication` `another means of communication` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 13(3) paragraph 3 applies to the communication` `another means of communication` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
--  ruler: the means, unsolicited, direct marketing, the national option, the subscriber or user has consented, does not wish to receive
#ASSERT `Art 13(3) the Directive requires the communication not to be allowed` `another means of communication` TRUE TRUE `consent of the subscriber or user is required` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- with consent, "not allowed without the consent" does not reach the communication
#ASSERT `Art 13(3) the Directive requires the communication not to be allowed` `another means of communication` TRUE TRUE `consent of the subscriber or user is required` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 13(3) the Directive requires the communication not to be allowed` `another means of communication` TRUE TRUE `subscribers or users who do not wish to receive the communications are protected` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the person has not said they do not wish to receive it: the option does not reach the communication
#ASSERT `Art 13(3) the Directive requires the communication not to be allowed` `another means of communication` TRUE TRUE `subscribers or users who do not wish to receive the communications are protected` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- national legislation's choice is outside the sources, but the overlap case is decided whichever option was chosen: no consent and the person does not wish to receive it (the first option prohibits it, so does the second)
#ASSERT `Art 13(3) the Directive requires the communication not to be allowed` `another means of communication` TRUE TRUE `national legislation has not been stated` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- option unstated, no consent, no objection: the first option prohibits it and the second does not, so the text does not decide it
#ASSERT `Art 13(3) the Directive requires the communication not to be allowed` `another means of communication` TRUE TRUE `national legislation has not been stated` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- option unstated, consent given and an objection too: consent answers the first option and the objection the second, so the text does not decide it
#ASSERT `Art 13(3) the Directive requires the communication not to be allowed` `another means of communication` TRUE TRUE `national legislation has not been stated` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- option unstated, consent given, no objection: neither option prohibits it, so the text does not prohibit it (limit of a prohibition in its own wording)
#ASSERT `Art 13(3) the Directive requires the communication not to be allowed` `another means of communication` TRUE TRUE `national legislation has not been stated` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the overlap case is limited to paragraph 3's subject: an e-mail is not paragraph 3's subject, and a message that is not unsolicited is not either
#ASSERT `Art 13(3) the Directive requires the communication not to be allowed` `an electronic mail message` TRUE TRUE `national legislation has not been stated` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 13(3) the Directive requires the communication not to be allowed` `another means of communication` FALSE TRUE `national legislation has not been stated` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- not paragraph 3's subject
#ASSERT `Art 13(3) the Directive requires the communication not to be allowed` `an electronic mail message` TRUE TRUE `consent of the subscriber or user is required` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 13(3) the Directive requires the communication not to be allowed` `another means of communication` FALSE TRUE `consent of the subscriber or user is required` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 13(3) the Directive requires the communication not to be allowed` `another means of communication` TRUE FALSE `consent of the subscriber or user is required` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 13(3) the option is free of charge for the subscriber or user` TRUE  EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 13(3) the option is free of charge for the subscriber or user` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Art 13(4)`
--  ruler: the means, direct marketing, disguises the sender, contravenes Art 6 of 2000/31/EC, no valid address, encourages visits to websites that contravene it
#ASSERT `Art 13(4) the practice of sending the electronic mail is prohibited` `an electronic mail message` TRUE TRUE  FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 13(4) the practice of sending the electronic mail is prohibited` `an electronic mail message` TRUE FALSE TRUE  FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 13(4) the practice of sending the electronic mail is prohibited` `an electronic mail message` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE  FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 13(4) the practice of sending the electronic mail is prohibited` `an electronic mail message` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE  EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 13(4) the practice of sending the electronic mail is prohibited` `an electronic mail message` TRUE TRUE  TRUE  TRUE  TRUE  EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- none of the four features: the paragraph does not say the message is allowed
#ASSERT `Art 13(4) the practice of sending the electronic mail is prohibited` `an electronic mail message` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- not electronic mail, or not direct marketing
#ASSERT `Art 13(4) the practice of sending the electronic mail is prohibited` `a facsimile machine` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 13(4) the practice of sending the electronic mail is prohibited` `an electronic mail message` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the regulative form
-- TRACE-EXPECT: BREACH
#TRACE `Art 13(4) the sender shall not send the electronic mail` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the sender` DOES `send direct marketing electronic mail` AT 3
-- TRACE-EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `Art 13(4) the sender shall not send the electronic mail` AT 0 WITH
    -- nothing sent: the prohibition stays standing

§ `Art 13(5)`
#ASSERT `Art 13(5) first sentence paragraphs 1 and 3 apply to the subscriber` TRUE  EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 13(5) first sentence paragraphs 1 and 3 apply to the subscriber` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 13(5) second sentence the Member State must ensure that the subscriber's legitimate interests with regard to unsolicited communications are sufficiently protected` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 13(5) second sentence the Member State must ensure that the subscriber's legitimate interests with regard to unsolicited communications are sufficiently protected` TRUE  EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Art 13(6)`
#ASSERT `Art 13(6) the legal proceedings leave the administrative remedy unaffected` TRUE  EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 13(6) the legal proceedings leave the administrative remedy unaffected` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
--  ruler: adversely affected, legitimate interest, an electronic communications service provider protecting its business interests
#ASSERT `Art 13(6) the person may bring legal proceedings in respect of the infringement` TRUE  TRUE  FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 13(6) the person may bring legal proceedings in respect of the infringement` TRUE  FALSE TRUE  EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 13(6) the person may bring legal proceedings in respect of the infringement` TRUE  FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 13(6) the person may bring legal proceedings in respect of the infringement` FALSE TRUE  FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 13(6) the person may bring legal proceedings in respect of the infringement` FALSE FALSE TRUE  EQUALS NOTHING
--  ruler: a provider of electronic communications services, contributes by its negligence
#ASSERT `Art 13(6) second sentence the Member State may lay down specific rules on penalties for the provider` TRUE  TRUE  EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 13(6) second sentence the Member State may lay down specific rules on penalties for the provider` TRUE  FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 13(6) second sentence the Member State may lay down specific rules on penalties for the provider` FALSE TRUE  EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Art 13 as a whole -- may this message be sent to this recipient?`
--  ruler: the means, direct marketing, unsolicited, natural person, consent, soft opt-in satisfied, a paragraph 4 feature, the national option, the recipient does not wish to receive
-- consent given, electronic mail: allowed
#ASSERT case `an electronic mail message` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `national legislation has not been stated` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no consent, soft opt-in satisfied: allowed
#ASSERT case `an electronic mail message` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE `national legislation has not been stated` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no consent, no soft opt-in: not allowed ("only")
#ASSERT case `an electronic mail message` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `national legislation has not been stated` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- paragraph 4 "in any event": a disguised sender is prohibited, whatever the consent or the soft opt-in
#ASSERT case `an electronic mail message` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE `national legislation has not been stated` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT case `an electronic mail message` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE `national legislation has not been stated` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- fax and automated calling: paragraph 1 alone
#ASSERT case `a facsimile machine` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `national legislation has not been stated` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT case `a facsimile machine` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE `national legislation has not been stated` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT case `an automated calling and communication system without human intervention` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `national legislation has not been stated` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT case `an automated calling and communication system without human intervention` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `national legislation has not been stated` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- paragraph 4 is about electronic mail only: a fax with the same feature is not caught by it
#ASSERT case `a facsimile machine` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE `national legislation has not been stated` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- other means (a call with a person): paragraph 3 and the national option
#ASSERT case `another means of communication` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `consent of the subscriber or user is required` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT case `another means of communication` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `consent of the subscriber or user is required` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT case `another means of communication` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `subscribers or users who do not wish to receive the communications are protected` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT case `another means of communication` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `subscribers or users who do not wish to receive the communications are protected` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- option unstated, but no consent and the recipient does not wish to receive it: both options prohibit it, so the message may not be sent
#ASSERT case `another means of communication` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `national legislation has not been stated` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- option unstated, no consent and no objection: the options differ, so the text does not decide it
#ASSERT case `another means of communication` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `national legislation has not been stated` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- option unstated, consent given and an objection too: the options differ, so the text does not decide it
#ASSERT case `another means of communication` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `national legislation has not been stated` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- a recipient that is not a natural person: paragraph 5 leaves paragraphs 1 and 3 aside
#ASSERT case `an electronic mail message` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `national legislation has not been stated` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT case `another means of communication` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `consent of the subscriber or user is required` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- ... but paragraph 4 applies "in any event"
#ASSERT case `an electronic mail message` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE `national legislation has not been stated` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not direct marketing: the Article is silent
#ASSERT case `an electronic mail message` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `national legislation has not been stated` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT case `another means of communication` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `consent of the subscriber or user is required` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- not unsolicited, other means: paragraph 3 does not apply
#ASSERT case `another means of communication` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `consent of the subscriber or user is required` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
